  {
   "slug": "speech-801669",
   "speaker": "Joe Ludwig",
   "party": "Labor",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2010-06-24",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "Government amendments to the Electoral Act redefined \"how-to-vote card\" by omitting previous paragraphs (b) and (c). Opposition amendments proposed allowing authorisation details at the top or bottom of cards and raising penalties from 10 to 50 penalty units (approximately $5,500). Senator Xenophon moved additional amendments to create an offence for misleading or deceptive conduct during elections, including powers for the Australian Electoral Commissioner to request desistance; these amendments were negatived."
